{"seq":16,"trial_id":"waterfall-frontier-2026-11/hermes-opus-none-mu-v03-dev/sy-01-quarrendon-ticket-numbers/r1","wall_ts":"2026-11-07T04:14:31.606Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:10:00-05:00","args_digest":"4990ed7bac102850493bb0dd3b0d7854c29c62abc6f6748fe1d083d6884a01e7","actor":"assistant","via":"mcp","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DWATERF0001","text":"Here's what I found. I went through all six of Moss's notes in the shared files (the North and Central team digests) and two Quarrendon Freight Lines ticket numbers come up:\n\n1. #PD-4492, from \"Moss: Sunday prep for Ruth\" (teams/team-north/digests/2025-10-05-north-sunday.md). Thea Ramaswell logged it on 4 Oct 2025: gatehouse kiosk SMS bay assignments weren't reaching drivers at Eau Claire Dock Doors 14-18 on the 04:00 shift. Support patched it that evening, and Thea confirmed on 5 Oct that it was fixed.\n2. #4419, from \"Moss: North cheat sheet (undated)\" (teams/team-north/digests/north-account-cheatsheet.md). Thea logged it about gatehouse barcode scanners not reading trailer tags at Door 14 on third shift. It was escalated to tier-2 for scanner firmware testing. The note has no date, so I can't say when it was raised or whether it's still open.\n\nNot included:\n- Moss's 9/14/2025 pipeline digest and 3/23/2026 renewal note both mention QFL but give no ticket numbers.\n- #4409, #4412 and FR-882 appear in the Central handoff digest, but they belong to Central accounts (Marrow), not QFL.\n- Marcus's note on \"Quarendon Freightways\" is about a different company that isn't our customer, and Moss didn't write it.\n\nI only looked at Moss's notes, not the #inc-qfl-sev1 channel. I can check that too if you want it covered."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DWATERF0001","ts":"1791987000.000124"}}
